  ],
  "text": "Switch gravity off for five seconds. The floating is not the part that kills you. Second one. Everything not bolted down simply lets go. Cars, people, whole crowds, drifting up at whatever speed they were already moving. The oceans lift too, in sheets. So does the air above them. And buildings only stand because their own weight presses them together. Take that away and the concrete quietly comes apart at the joints. Then the five seconds end. And everything that rose comes back down at the same moment. The floating never hurt anyone. The landing does. And the air that drifted away does not politely come back. Gravity is not holding you down. It is holding everything together. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
